## reading
- Entry (5): the scan script that produced the 1000-4000 output was saved at 16:24:15, the pre-registration was
  committed at 16:24:16, the output was written at 16:25:05, and the run takes 43.4 s here. So the run started at
  about 16:24:21, after the commit.
- Entries (3) and (4): the binaries that produce the predicted quantities were compiled at 16:07:50 (twin sieve) and
  16:08:25 (2e9 and 5e9 height sums), after the commit at 16:07:04. The earlier binaries stop at 1e9 and contain no
  twin data.
- Caveat: the uniform 16:21:58 mtimes are copy times, not run times; the binary compile times are the binding
  evidence.
